LICENSE SPLIT
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not everything in this repository carries the same license (decision 0015):

  Code (src/, tools/, tests/)         Apache-2.0        LICENSE
  Source registry (sources/)          CC0-1.0           sources/LICENSE
  Documentation prose (*.md, docs/)   CC-BY-4.0         docs/LICENSE
  Recorded responses (tests/fixtures) the publisher's own terms; see
                                      THIRD_PARTY_DATA.yml

The registry is CC0 so that the inventory it encodes — which sources exist,
who stewards them, what their terms say — can be lifted wholesale by anyone
building a different thing, including DOE itself.

REDISTRIBUTED CONTENT
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recorded API responses under tests/fixtures/ are government-published
content retrieved from the endpoints named in THIRD_PARTY_DATA.yml. Each
entry there records the publisher, the retrieval date, the rights the
publisher asserts, and any attribution the publisher requires. Most US
government works are not subject to copyright in the United States
(17 U.S.C. § 105), but that is not universal across this ecosystem: some
DOE-hosted content is contributed by universities, foreign institutions, or
contractors under their own terms. The file records the difference rather
than assuming it away.

LINEAGE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
DOE-MCP's packaging shape is borrowed, deliberately and with thanks, from
PNNL's NEPA-MCP: one pip package with many focused stdio servers over a
shared library, and the doctor/configure CLI. NEPA-MCP is a product of
Pacific Northwest National Laboratory. This project is not affiliated with
it, and the attribution is a statement about influence rather than about
endorsement.
